## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant isolation, data residency, idempotency, observability, and cost-conscious design in a fintech data-bridge.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub per-tenant isolation
- Dataflow streaming with dedupe
- BigQuery per-tenant datasets with partitioning
- IAM least privilege and per-tenant service accounts
- Data residency and cost controls
- Observability with Cloud Logging/Monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow-like transform
function process(event) {
  if (!event || !event.id) return;
  if (!seen.has(event.id)) {
    writeBigQuery(event);
    seen.add(event.id);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant isolation at scale?
- How would you handle late-arriving data and replays?
- What are your rollback/disaster-recovery considerations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical Dataflow streaming design with real-world concerns like per-tenant isolation and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub ingestion
- Dataflow streaming transforms and DoFn-like validation
- Per-tenant BigQuery datasets and environment isolation
- Idempotency/dedup and basic monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Dataflow DoFn for validation
function validateEvent(record){
  if(!record.event_id || !record.tenant_id) throw new Error("Invalid");
  if(!record.event_ts) record.event_ts = Date.now();
  return record;
}
```

